{question}

{choices}

Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.3. Evaluation Criteria. <omitted> (a) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, at any time prior to the Closing Date, the Company Board may effect a Company Adverse Recommendation Change <omitted> if, and only if, <omitted> (ii) the Company Board, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and a financial advisor of nationally recognized reputation, determines in good faith that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with its fiduciary duties under applicable Law, (iii) the Company has provided Parent with written notice of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the seventh Business Day after Parent receives such written notice, (iv) if not in connection with an Intervening Event pursuant to Section 8.3(b), the decision to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change is in connection with an Acquisition Proposal that the Company Board, after consultation with its outside financial advisor, determines constitutes a Superior Proposal, and the Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (6), as follows: (1) the Company Board shall have determined that such Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal after considering the financial aspects of the proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal, (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent, during the seven Business Day period provided in clause (iii) of this Section 8.3(a), to make adjustments to this Agreement so that the Acquisition Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, that such Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, (5) the Company Board shall have consulted with a regulatory compliance advisor to ensure that the proposal meets all applicable regulatory standards, (6) if the Company intends to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, the Company shall have complied with Section 10.1(d)(i). For clarity, the provisions of this Section 8.3(a) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal (except that any reference to seven Business Days shall instead be four Business Days) or any successive Acquisition Proposals. (Pages 81-82)\nAnswer:
Choices:

