Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: ARTICLE 8. No Solicitation. <omitted> (f) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, during the Pre-Closing Period, the Company Board may change its recommendation if, and only if, (i) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and financial advisors, that the failure to change the recommendation would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (ii) the Company has provided Parent with written notice of the Company Board’s intention to change the recommendation at least five Business Days in advance, (iii) the Company Board has determined that an Acquisition Proposal constitutes a Superior Proposal based primarily on the financial terms offered, and (iv) the Company shall have complied with its obligations to negotiate with Parent in good faith to adjust the terms of the current Agreement to make it financially superior, if possible. Any amendment to the financial terms of an Acquisition Proposal shall require a new determination and notice period as specified herein. (Pages 88-89)
